{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TUIkit provides a focus system that lets users move between interactive views (buttons, menus, text fields) using Tab, Shift+Tab, or arrow keys. The system consists of three parts:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FocusManager"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Tracks which element is focused, handles navigation"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Focusable","type":"reference","isActive":true}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Protocol that views adopt to receive focus","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusState","type":"reference","isActive":true}]},{"type":"text","text":": Lightweight state object that views use to query and request focus"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","text":"How Focus Works","anchor":"How-Focus-Works","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every frame, the ","type":"text"},{"code":"FocusManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is cleared and interactive views re-register themselves during rendering. This means focus registrations are always in sync with the current view tree: removed views are automatically unregistered.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The focus order follows the rendering order: the first focusable view rendered is first in the Tab cycle.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"The Focusable Protocol","anchor":"The-Focusable-Protocol","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Views that want to receive focus conform to ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Focusable","isActive":true},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public protocol Focusable: AnyObject {","    var focusID: String { get }","    var canBeFocused: Bool { get }","    func onFocusReceived()","    func onFocusLost()","    func handleKeyEvent(_ event: KeyEvent) -> Bool","}"]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"focusID"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Unique identifier for this focusable element","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"canBeFocused"}]},{"text":": Whether focus can move to this element (default: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"text":")","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"onFocusReceived()","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Called when this element gains focus (default: no-op)"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"onFocusLost()","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Called when this element loses focus (default: no-op)","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"handleKeyEvent(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": Handle a key event while focused; return "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" if consumed"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A default extension provides sensible defaults for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"canBeFocused"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":"), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onFocusReceived()"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onFocusLost()"},{"type":"text","text":" (both no-ops). Only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"focusID"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"handleKeyEvent(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" must be implemented."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Using FocusState","anchor":"Using-FocusState","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusState","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is the user-facing API for checking and requesting focus inside a view:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let focusState = FocusState(id: \"my-button\", focusManager: context.environment.focusManager)","","\/\/ Check if this element is currently focused","if focusState.isFocused {","    \/\/ render with focus indicator","}","","\/\/ Programmatically request focus","focusState.requestFocus()"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Built-in views like ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Button","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Menu","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" create their own ","type":"text"},{"code":"FocusState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" internally: you only need it when building custom focusable views.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Navigation Keys","anchor":"Navigation-Keys","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FocusManager"},{"text":" responds to these keys during dispatch:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Action"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tab"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Move focus to the next element","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Shift+Tab","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Move focus to the previous element","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Arrow Down \/ Right","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Move focus to the next element"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Arrow Up \/ Left"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Move focus to the previous element"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"type":"heading","text":"FocusRegistration Helper","anchor":"FocusRegistration-Helper","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Built-in interactive views use the internal ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FocusRegistration"},{"text":" helper to avoid boilerplate. It handles three tasks in one call:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist a focus ID"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" via ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateStorage"},{"text":" so it remains stable across renders","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Register","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the handler with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FocusManager"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Query"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" whether this view currently has focus"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Custom views that implement "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Focusable"},{"type":"text","text":" typically do not need "},{"code":"FocusRegistration","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" directly. It is used by the framework’s "},{"code":"_*Core","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" views (e.g. "},{"code":"_ButtonCore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"_ListCore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Focus Indicator","anchor":"Focus-Indicator","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The visual indicator depends on the view type. Buttons and similar controls use a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"highlight background bar"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" for the focused item. Text fields use ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"pulsing vertical bars"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (caps) around the input area. Lists and tables use a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"highlight background","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" for the focused row, with a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"pulsing accent background","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" when the row is both focused and selected.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Focus in the Event Loop","anchor":"Focus-in-the-Event-Loop","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Focus dispatch happens in Layer 2 of the key event pipeline (see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/AppLifecycle","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"):"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A key event arrives from stdin"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Layer 1 (status bar) gets first chance to handle it"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Layer 2: ","type":"text"},{"code":"KeyEventDispatcher","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" dispatches to the focused view’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"handleKeyEvent(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If not consumed, navigation keys (Tab, arrows) are handled by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FocusManager"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Layer 3 (default bindings) handles quit, theme cycling, etc.","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusSystem"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tuikit\/focussystem"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"article","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Focus System","modules":[{"name":"TUIkit"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Navigate between interactive elements using the keyboard."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StateManagement","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ThemingGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/AppearanceAndColors","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Preferences","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/CustomViews","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/KeyboardShortcuts","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PaletteReference","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ListAndTable","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/LayoutSystem"],"anchor":"Guides","generated":true,"title":"Guides"}],"references":{"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/ListAndTable":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ListAndTable","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/listandtable","title":"List and Table Components","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build scrollable, navigable data collections with keyboard support."}]},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/StateManagement":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StateManagement","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"State Management","abstract":[{"text":"Manage reactive state in your TUIkit application.","type":"text"}],"ur